<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ruyan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Rustamdar, Rostamdar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ruyan was a mountainous region of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabaristan">Tabaristan</a>, on the northern slopes of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alborz">Alborz</a> in what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mazandaran">Mazandaran</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, later known as Rustamdar. Its local princes, above all the Paduspanids, kept power there for centuries under successive overlords, and in 864 its people invited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hasan-ibn-zayd">Hasan ibn Zayd</a> to lead the revolt that founded the Alavid state.</p></div>
